[00:00.06]Two thousand years ago
{"两千年前"}
[00:06.18]Two thousand years ago
{"两千年前"}
[00:14.13]Two thousand years ago
{"两千年前"}
[00:14.45]
[00:14.84]The proudest boast was "civis Romanus sum."
{"最骄傲的宣言是「我是罗马公民」"}
[00:22.85]
[00:23.03]Today, in the world of freedom the proudest boast is "Ich bin ein Berliner.
{"如今在自由世界最骄傲的宣言是「我是柏林人」"}
[00:45.96]Ich bin ein Berliner.
{"我是柏林人。"}
[01:02.58]
[01:17.77]Berlin
{"柏林"}
[01:22.39]
[01:31.85]Ich bin ein Berliner.
{"我是柏林人。"}
[01:34.54]
[02:07.42]Freedom has many difficulties and democracy is not perfect,
{"自由充满艰难民主亦非完美"}
[02:18.94]but we have never had to put a wall up to keep our people in,
{"但我们从未需要筑墙禁锢人民"}
[02:22.90]
[02:49.42]I know of no town, no city,
{"我未曾见过任何城镇"}
[02:53.17]
[02:53.88]that has been besieged for 18 years that still lives with the vitality and the force,
{"在被围困十八年后仍能保有西柏林这般活力"}
[03:03.68]
[03:04.14]and the hope and the determination of the city of West Berlin.
{"力量与希望以及决心"}
[03:11.24]
[03:24.03]Ich bin ein Berliner.
{"我是柏林人。"}
